# The sprites are published to their own host and served from there,
# so Vercel never needs them. They are the most requested thing the
# game has by a wide margin, and every request for one would otherwise
# be counted against the app's own allowance.
#
# Vite copies public/ into the build output, so keeping the files out
# of the upload keeps them out of the deployment. Development is
# untouched: the files stay in the working tree and Vite serves them.
public/sprites

# The sprite host's own config, which the app's build has no use for
wrangler.jsonc
